class:: HarmonicDeviation
summary:: Harmonic amplitude deviation from a local envelope
categories:: UGens>Analysis>Tonal
related:: Guides/MIRa, Classes/HPCP, Classes/HarmonicPeaks, Classes/HarmonicVariation, Classes/HarmonicCentroid, Classes/Pitch2

description::
Shared interpolated spectral peaks are associated with the nearest integer harmonic of the supplied F0. Only the strongest matching peak occupies each harmonic slot. Missing harmonics retain zero slots; an incorrect F0 or tight tolerance changes the result. The formulas are explicit MIRa conventions in the harmonic-descriptor tradition summarized by Peeters (2004); this is independent code, not a wrapper around another analysis library. For each nonzero harmonic amplitude a, the envelope is the arithmetic mean of its preceding, current and following harmonic amplitudes. At boundaries the current amplitude substitutes for the absent neighbour. Output is the amplitude-weighted mean absolute value of 20*log10(a/envelope). Missing internal slots count as zero in the envelope.



classmethods::
method:: kr
argument:: chain
FFT chain. This analyzer updates when a new frame arrives and holds its output between frames.

argument:: f0
Supplied fundamental in Hz, for example the first output of Pitch2. Nonpositive or invalid values disable harmonic association.

argument:: maxHarmonics
Literal number of harmonic slots from 1 through 64. Harmonic index is stable when partials are missing.

argument:: tolerance
Maximum distance in cents between a peak and its nearest integer multiple of f0, clamped from 0 through 600. Default 50.

argument:: peakThreshold
Minimum local-peak magnitude relative to the largest included spectral peak, from 0 through 1. Up to 128 strongest peaks are retained.

argument:: fftSize
Literal power of two from 256 through 8192, matching the FFT buffer. Frequency resolution and first-result latency depend on this size.

returns::
Nonnegative weighted deviation in dB; zero without associated peaks.

method:: fromAudio
Convenience constructor: accepts audio and builds Pitch2 plus FFT internally, then calls kr with the estimated F0. The input range defaults to 55 through 1760 Hz, FFT size 4096 and hop fraction 0.25; it accepts the same harmonic controls. Use kr when sharing an existing pitch estimate or FFT chain.

examples::
HarmonicDeviation measures how much the harmonic spectral envelope deviates from a smooth moving-average contour. In this example, it drives an adaptive stereo flanger: jagged, irregular spectral envelopes increase flanging depth and feedback, imparting comb filtering movement whenever timbre becomes complex. An interactive code::MIRaGUI.scope:: tracks the real-time deviation metric.
code::
(
s.waitForBoot({
    var path = MIRaGUI.soundPath("melody.wav");
    ~miraBuffer = if(path.notNil) { Buffer.read(s, path) } { nil };
    ~miraBus = Bus.control(s, 1);
    s.sync;
    ~miraExample = {
        var source = if(~miraBuffer.notNil) {
            PlayBuf.ar(1, ~miraBuffer, BufRateScale.kr(~miraBuffer), loop: 1)
        } {
            // Synthetic melody fallback
            Saw.ar(Select.kr(LFNoise0.kr(2).range(0, 5), [220, 261.63, 293.66, 329.63, 392, 440])) * 0.2
        };
        // For live input instead: source = SoundIn.ar(0);

        var pitch = PitchMPM.kr(source, 80, 1600, 2048, 0.25);
        var chain = FFT(LocalBuf(2048), source, 0.25);
        var dev = HarmonicDeviation.kr(chain, pitch[0], maxHarmonics: 16, fftSize: 2048);
        var devSmooth = dev.lag(0.04);

        // Flanger depth modulated by spectral deviation
        var flangerMod = SinOsc.kr(0.3 + (devSmooth * 1.5), [0, pi/2], 0.002, 0.005);
        var flanger = CombC.ar(source, 0.02, flangerMod, 0.2 + (devSmooth * 0.4).clip(0, 0.8));
        var sound = (source * 0.25 ! 2) + (flanger * 0.2);

        if(~miraBus.notNil) { Out.kr(~miraBus, dev) };
        sound * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.2)
    }.play;

    ~miraGUI = MIRaGUI.scope("Harmonic Deviation", ~miraBus, 0.0, 1.0);
});
)
::
code::
(
~miraExample.free;
if(~miraGUI.notNil) { ~miraGUI.close };
if(~miraBus.notNil) { ~miraBus.free };
if(~miraBuffer.notNil) { ~miraBuffer.free };
)
::
